                <Placemark>
                    <name>Albert Edward Arber</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Albert Edward Arber<br>In memory of Auxiliary Fireman Albert Edward Arber who served under Station 32 Bow and who died as a result of enemy action buried by falling masonry at the junction of St Stephens Road and Athelstane Grove on the night of 19th/20th March 1941 when a high explosive bomb demolished two houses near this site<br>Athelstane Grove, Bow<br>Firemen Remembered 2004]]></description>
