                <Placemark>
                    <name>Thomas Briggs</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Thomas Briggs<br>129 Cadogan Terrace. A memorial to Thomas Briggs Esq. of Clapton who on Saturday 9th July 1864 was viciously assaulted near here on a North London railway train. Carried near to death into this public house he died at home later the same day. He was the first person to be murdered on a railway train.<br>129 Cadogan Terrace, Bow<br>Bow Neighbourhood]]></description>
                    <Point>
