            <Folder>
                <name>Brugess Park</name>
                <Placemark>
                    <name>Sir Robert Hunter</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Sir Robert Hunter<br>Addington Square was built between 1810 and 1850, when the area was still mostly fields and market gardens. It became home to the well-to-do escaping densely populated central London. It had two swimming baths by 1840. In 1844, National Trust founder Robert Hunter was born. The Richardsons gang operated here in the 1960's.<br>Addington Square, Brugess Park<br>Friends of Burgess Park]]></description>
