                </Placemark>
                <Placemark>
                    <name>Grand Surrey Canal</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Grand Surrey Canal<br>The Grand Surrey Canal was started in 1801, with great plans to link fast-developing docks at Rotherhithe with Mitcham and Portsmouth. It opened as far as Camberwell Road in 1811, later reaching Croydon and Peckham, and formed a useful industrial artery for all kinds of goods and materials, finally closing in 1970.<br>Sumner Road, Burgess Park<br>Friends of Burgess Park]]></description>
