                    <name>Wisteria</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Wisteria<br>Wisteria This iconic wisteria is one of the oldest specimens in the country. Brought here from China in 1816, a year after the Battle of Waterloo, It was planted in the brewery yard outside what was then the Head Brewer's house. It flourished and remains a focal point for visitors.<br>Chiswick Lane South<br>Fuller's Brewery]]></description>
