                <Placemark>
                    <name>Vincent Crane Richmond</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Vincent Crane Richmond<br>Lt. Col. Vincent C Richmond OBE 1893-1930. The designer of the ill-fated R101 airship lived here as a boy, attending the nearby Selwyn Avenue school. He was one of 48 who perished when the R101 crashed near Beauvais, France in October 1930. Richmond Crescent was named in his honour<br>24 Silverdale Road, Highams Park E4<br>London]]></description>
