                <Placemark>
                    <name>plaque № 9678</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[plaque № 9678<br>The Bull and Crown. Grade II Listed building - Erected in 1899 by Taylor Walker and Company and designed in French Second Empire style. It was built to cater for the vast influx of visitors to the nearby Epping Forest and replaced an earlier 18th century inn<br>The Bull on the Green, The Green, Chingford E4<br>London]]></description>
