                <Placemark>
                    <name>Ralph Steadman and Hunter S. Thompson</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Ralph Steadman and Hunter S. Thompson<br>In this house in the summer of 1971, the artist Ralph Steadman (1936-2036) poured his soul out onto paper to liberate the evil demons from a manuscript by Hunter S. Thompson, entitled 'Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas: A savage journey into the heart of the American dream' Res Ipsa Loquitur<br>103 New Kings Road, Fulham<br>Morganico.com]]></description>
                    <Point>
