                <Placemark>
                    <name>Malcolm Campbell</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Malcolm Campbell<br>101 Farm Lane This site was first developed in the 1890s as a horse bus company depot. It was then used by various motor bus companies and by the British Motor Cab Co., who probably built the double-arched entrance around 1910. Sir Malcolm Campbell, holder of land and water speed records, operated an aircraft engineering firm from here in the 1920s.<br>Farm Lane, Fulham<br>Hammersmith and Fulham Historic Buildings Group 2015]]></description>
                    <Point>
                        <coordinates>-0.19689,51.48339,0</coordinates>
