                    <description><![CDATA[Matilda Sharpe, Channing School, and Emily Sharpe<br>Matilda and Emily Sharpe 1842-1928 Matilda was a teacher, educational reformer, author and painter and with her sister, Emily, established Channing School in 1885 to educate the daughters of Unitarian ministers and others. Several of her works can be found in the National Portrait Gallery.<br>Channing School, The Bank, Highgate<br>Highgate Heritage 2019]]></description>
