                    <description><![CDATA[John Hargrave Stevens, George Alexander, and 2 others<br>St. Johns Church was built in 1845 in the early English Gothic style by John Hargrave Stevens and George Alexander. This site on the summit of Notting Hill had formerly been a view-point for spectators at the centre of the Hippodrome race course.<br>Lansdowne Crescent<br>Royal Borough of Kensington &amp; Chelsea]]></description>
