                <Placemark>
                    <name>Horatio Nelson and Emma Hamilton</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Horatio Nelson and Emma Hamilton<br>Merton Place. Sixty metres (200 feet) to the south east was ‘Merton Place’, the only house ever owned (1801 – 1805) by Admiral Lord Nelson and from which he set out for the Battle of trafalgar. Lady Hamilton also lived here 1801 – 1808.<br>Merton Place, nr Doel Close, Merton<br>London]]></description>
                    <Point>
                        <coordinates>-0.18818,51.4148,0</coordinates>
                    </Point>
                    <LookAt>
                        <longitude>-0.18818</longitude>
