                <Placemark>
                    <name>Charles Dickens, John Rennie, John Rennie, and 2 others</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Charles Dickens, John Rennie, John Rennie, and 2 others<br>These steps and arch are surviving fragments of the 1831 London Bridge designed by John Rennie and built by his son Sir John Rennie. These steps were the scene of the murder of Nancy in Charles Dickens' novel Oliver Twist.<br>Montague Close<br>London]]></description>
