                <Placemark>
                    <name>Marc Isambard Brunel, Isambard Kingdom Brunel, and Thames Tunnel</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Marc Isambard Brunel, Isambard Kingdom Brunel, and Thames Tunnel<br>Near this spot in 1828 Isambard Kingdom Brunel was pulled half-drowned from the flooded shaft. The Thames Tunnel was abandoned for seven years and Marc Brunel sent his son to Clifton to convalesce...<br>Rotherhithe Street<br>London]]></description>
                    <Point>
