                <Placemark>
                    <name>Peter II and Henry III</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Peter II and Henry III<br>Within these precincts stood the Palace of Savoy, the erection of which was begun by Peter, ninth Count of Savoy and Earl of Richmond, A.D 1246. Henry III King of England bestowed the site "in vico qui vocato la straunde" on February 12th 1246 and there was erected a palace, "the fayrest mannor in Europe" big enough for a large part of an army<br>Savoy Court<br>London]]></description>
