                    <description><![CDATA[Anne Hyde, James II, and Savoy<br>On part of this site in 1640 was built Worcester House where lived Edward second Marquess of Worcester. At midnight on the 3rd. September, 1660, Anne Hyde daughter of the Earl of Clarendon was secretly married here to the Duke of York (afterwards James II) whose two daughters, Mary and Anne, became Queens of England.<br>Savoy Court<br>London]]></description>
