                <Placemark>
                    <name>Burtt &amp; Sons</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Burtt &amp; Sons<br>The Lime Kiln was built in 1816 by builders' suppliers Burtt &amp; Sons, and is now Grade II listed. Coal and limestone brought along the canal were burnt for 3 days to produce quicklime, a key ingredient of mortar for houses and fertilizer for agriculture. As 'limelight' it was used to illuminate Victorian theatres.<br>Albany Road<br>Friends of Burgess Park]]></description>
