                <Placemark>
                    <name>Palingswick House, Barnabas Steel, and Kensington &amp; Chelsea Board of Guardians School</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Palingswick House, Barnabas Steel, and Kensington &amp; Chelsea Board of Guardians School<br>Palingswick House was built in the 19th century as a private residence, possibly for Barnabas Steel, whose initials appear on the façade. By the 1880 it was in institutional use, first as a Kensington &amp; Chelsea Board of Guardians School and then as a home for diabetic children. The house was renamed after the old manor of Palingswick in 1954.<br>West London Free School Palingswick House 241 King Street<br>Hammersmith and Fulham Historic Buildings Group]]></description>
