                <Placemark>
                    <name>Hammersmith Palais</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Hammersmith Palais<br>HAMMERSMITH PALAIS opened as a roller skating rink in 1910. Later it served as an ice rink and, most famously as a 'palais de danse' with a capacity of 2,500. Dancing continued all through the Second World War despite the Blitz. From the 1960s the Palais was increasingly used for live concerts and club nights. It finally closed in 2007.<br>228 Shepherds Bush Road<br>Hammersmith and Fulham Historic Buildings Group 2014]]></description>
