                </Placemark>
                <Placemark>
                    <name>Great storm</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Great storm<br>In the early hours of Friday 16 October 1987 a great storm struck South East England. In four violent hours London lost 250,000 trees. Its skyline changed for ever. The Evening Standard launched a tree appeal and this English oak, placed here a year after the storm, is one of the many new trees paid for by its readers. It was planted by the City of Westminster on 16 October 1988.<br>Gate pillar at junction of Strand and Villiers Street<br>The Evening Standard 1988]]></description>
