                <Placemark>
                    <name>London Pavilion</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[London Pavilion<br>London Pavilion On this site between 1885 and 1934 stood the re-sited London Pavilion built following the demolition of its predecessor in Tichborne Street. The first West End theatre to introduce the now familiar "tip-up" seats, the London Pavilion was converted into a cinema in 1934, and a retail and entertainment centre in 1988<br>Piccadilly Circus<br>Society of West End Theatre]]></description>
