                    <description><![CDATA[William Barber<br>This building, designed by Ernest George &amp; Peto, was built for Judge William Barber of Barrow Point House as a temperance tavern in 1878. Its tea - garden attracted visitors from London. It flourished until the late 1920s as Ye Cocoa Tree, then became the local Conservative club until the 1960s.<br>64 High Street, Pinner<br>Harrow Heritage Trust]]></description>
