                <Placemark>
                    <name>King Edward III</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[King Edward III<br>A Half-Pint History The Queen's Head is Pinner's oldest inn. Records show there has been an inn on the site since 1540, although there is a theory that there was an Ale House here When King Edward Ill signed The Royal Charter to create Pinner's Annual Fair in 1336. During the 16th and 17th centuries the inn was called The Crown, and only in 1715 was it renamed The Queen's Head.<br>31 High St, Pinner<br>London]]></description>
