                <Placemark>
                    <name>Hammersmith Drawdock and Beckett's Wharf</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Hammersmith Drawdock and Beckett's Wharf<br>Hammersmith Drawdock Hammersmith Drawdock and Beckett's Wharf were, in the 18th Century, important transport links for Hammersmith. Goods such as hay and coal were brought by barge and off-loaded to horse drawn carts on the foreshore for local delivery via Queen Caroline Street to Hammersmith. Today the drawdock is still an important river access point.<br>Riverside Studios, 101 Queen Caroline Street London Hammersmith<br>Hammersmith and Fulham Historic Buildings Group 2018]]></description>
