                <Placemark>
                    <name>Samuel Pepys, Elizabeth I of England, John Evelyn, and 3 others</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Samuel Pepys, Elizabeth I of England, John Evelyn, and 3 others<br>On this site was built the Davies Amphitheatre 1662-1682 the last bear-baiting ring of Bankside visited by Samuel Pepys and John Evelyn. To the north from mid 16th century was the Bear Gardens, a bear-baiting ring visited by Queen Elizabeth I and replaced by The Hope Playhouse 1614-1656, built for plays and bear-baiting where Ben Jonson's play 'Bartholomew Fair' was first performed<br>Bear Gardens, SE1<br>London Borough of Southwark]]></description>
