                <Placemark>
                    <name>plaque № 8962</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[plaque № 8962<br>Thames Barrier Officially opened in 1984, it is the world's largest navigable flood barrier and incorporated novel and unique engineering design and operation of equipment. It is vital and effective in London's flood defences as well as being one of the capital's aesthetically pleasing major structures. Project sponsored by the Greater London Council Consulting engineers Rendel Palmer and Tritton. Operated by the National Rivers Authority.<br>Thames Barrier Learning Centre, 1 Unity Way, Woolwich SE18<br>Institution of Mechanical Engineers 1991]]></description>
