                <Placemark>
                    <name>Hans Sloane and Henry VIII</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[Hans Sloane and Henry VIII<br>King Henry VIII’s Manor House stood here until 1753 when it was demolished after the death of its last occupant, Sir Hans Sloane. Nos. 19 to 26 Cheyne Walk were built on its site in 1759-65. The old manor house garden still lies beyond the end wall of Cheyne Mews and contains some mulberry trees said to have been planted by Queen Elizabeth I.<br>23 Cheyne Walk, Chelsea, SW3<br>Royal Borough of Kensington &amp; Chelsea]]></description>
