                    <description><![CDATA[John Fielding, Bow Street, London, Henry Fielding, and 2 others<br>Bow Street was formed about 1637. It has been the residence of many notable men, among whom were Henry Fielding (novelist), Sir John Fielding (magistrate), Grinling Gibbons (woodcarver), Charles Macklin (actor), John Radcliffe (physician), Charles Sackville Earl of Dorset (poet), William Wycherley (dramatist)<br>19-20 Bow Street, Westminster, WC2<br>Administered by English Heritage as part of the London wide plaque scheme 1929]]></description>
