                <Placemark>
                    <name>David Garrick, George Bernard Shaw, Robert Adam, and 4 others</name>
                    <description><![CDATA[David Garrick, George Bernard Shaw, Robert Adam, and 4 others<br>This building stands on the site of Adelphi Terrace built by the brothers Adam in 1768-1774. Among the occupants of the Terrace were Topham and Lady Diana Beauclerk, David Garrick, Richard Doyle Carte, Thomas Hardy &amp; George Bernard Shaw, The London School of Economics and Political Science and the Savage Club also had their premises here.<br>The Adelphi, Westminster, WC2<br>Administered by English Heritage as part of the London wide plaque scheme 1952]]></description>
